meta {
  name: Send partner with us email
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/send-links/partners
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "partner@example.com",
    "name": "Jane Doe",
    "option": ["CO_HOST_PROGRAMS", "SPONSOR_INITIATIVES"]
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

docs {
  # Send Partner With Us Email
  
  Submits a partnership request from the website. The service renders a `partner-with-cedar.ejs` email template with the requester's details and sends it to the Cedarrise admin inbox. It also emits a `SEND_PARTNER_REQUEST_EMAIL` event to update the necessary counters.
  
  ## Endpoint
  `POST /api/v1/send-links/partners`
  
  ## Request Body
  The request expects a JSON object with the following fields:
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Constraints | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `email` | string | Yes | Must be a valid email address | The email address of the person requesting a partnership. |
  | `name` | string | Yes | Min: 3 characters, Max: 256 characters | The name of the person requesting a partnership. |
  | `option` | string[] | Yes | Array of allowed enum values (see below) | The partnership areas the requester is interested in. |
  
  ### Allowed `option` Values
  | Value | Description |
  | :--- | :--- |
  | `CO_HOST_PROGRAMS` | Co-host programs with Cedarrise. |
  | `PROVIDE_RESOURCES` | Provide resources to initiatives. |
  | `SPONSOR_INITIATIVES` | Sponsor Cedarrise initiatives. |
  | `OFFER_EXPERTISE` | Offer professional expertise. |
  | `OTHER` | Other partnership interest. |
  
  ## Success Response
  - **Status Code**: `200 OK`
  - **Body**:
    ```json
    {
      "success": true,
      "message": "Partner request email sent successfully",
      "meta": {
        "correlationId": "uuid-v4-string"
      }
    }
    ```
  
  ## Error Responses
  - **400 Bad Request**: Validation failed (e.g., invalid email, name too short, invalid `option` enum value).
  - **429 Too Many Requests**: Rate limit exceeded (`sendLinksLimiter`: 5 requests per 15-minute window, keyed by IP).
  - **500 Internal Server Error**: 
    - Failed to render the EJS email template.
    - Brevo API error (email transporter failure).
    - Email delivery verification failed — thrown when `sendEmail` returns a falsy value (`"Partner With us Email was not sent"`).
  
  ## Rate Limiting
  This endpoint is protected by `sendLinksLimiter` — a maximum of **5 requests per 15-minute window**, keyed by the client's IP address. Exceeds return a `429` with `{ code: "RATE_LIMITED", message: "Too many request attempts. Please try again later" }`.
  
  ## Side Effects
  - Emits `GENERAL_EVENTS.SEND_PARTNER_REQUEST_EMAIL` with `{ newPartnersCount: 1 }`, which triggers counter updates.
  
  ## Notes
  - The email is sent to a hardcoded admin address, not to the requester.
  - The `option` array is passed to the EJS template as `partnerAreas`.
  - No caching is involved — this endpoint triggers a transactional email on every call.
}
